    <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{"@type": "Question", "name": "What is the single highest-ROI channel for a local courier company?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Google Business Profile + local pack SEO. Zero marginal channel cost, high-intent buyers, and reviews compound trust. Most local courier operators under-invest in GBP optimisation and leave 30-50% of their local intent traffic on the table. We prioritise this in Phase 2 of every engagement."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How do local courier companies compete against Delhivery, Blue Dart and DTDC on Google?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "You do not compete for brand + national terms. You win on city + service + niche terms: \"D2C courier Bhiwandi\", \"same-day delivery Whitefield\", \"documents courier Andheri\". These win on local + long-tail SEO + Google Business Profile without needing D2C-scale ad budgets."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Should a courier company advertise on Meta (Facebook + Instagram)?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes, if your customer includes D2C brand founders or small businesses. Meta targeting Shopify + WooCommerce merchants + Meta lookalikes on your best existing D2C clients is highly effective. Click-to-WhatsApp click-to-message ads reduce CPL by 30-40% vs form-fill for D2C 3PL and courier operators."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How does a courier company use WhatsApp for marketing?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Three ways: (1) Click-to-message ads for lead capture from Meta + Google; (2) Booking + tracking + rate-broadcast + cross-sell flows via WhatsApp Cloud API + Interakt / AiSensy; (3) Automated review generation loop after every booking. This alone lifts NRR (net revenue retention) 20-40% on the existing customer book."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What is the CPL benchmark for courier leads on Google + Meta?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Local courier enquiry Rs 60-200 per lead on Google Search Ads. D2C courier / 3PL enquiry Rs 350-800. Meta Ads for D2C-founder targeting Rs 400-1,200. Meta click-to-WhatsApp Rs 250-600. These are directional; SQL cost (qualified pipeline) is what matters for the P&amp;L."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How long does it take to see leads from courier company digital marketing?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Google Business Profile + local pack: 30-45 days to visible movement. Paid channels: first leads in 5-10 days. SEO + content: month 3-4 for meaningful non-brand traffic. WhatsApp: immediate on launch of first broadcast. 60-80 leads / month is realistic for a well-executed 90-day launch on a mid-market local courier operator."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Do you help with franchise + partner marketing?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. For franchise networks, we build dedicated franchise-partner lead pages, multi-region SEO for hub coverage, partner-portal content, and franchise-onboarding funnels. Different funnel from customer acquisition; different KPIs; requires its own landing pages + creative + qualification form."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "Can you handle international courier + cross-border marketing?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Yes. India-to-GCC + India-to-USA + India-to-UK cross-border courier operators + document + parcel specialists. See our related freight-forwarding marketing page for the enterprise-B2B side; for D2C-facing international courier we mix Meta + WhatsApp with LinkedIn ABM."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "What is the biggest mistake local courier companies make with marketing?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Investing heavily in generic display + video ads before nailing Google Business Profile + local pack + review generation. Local courier is a discovery + trust business, not a brand-awareness business. Discovery + trust are cheaper + faster + more durable than paid awareness."}}, {"@type": "Question", "name": "How much should a local courier company spend on digital marketing?", "acceptedAnswer": {"@type": "Answer", "text": "Rs 1.5-3.5 lakh per month all-in for a founder-led local courier (Rs 3-20 Cr revenue). Rs 4-12 lakh for mid-market (Rs 20-150 Cr). Rs 12-40 lakh+ for enterprise + multi-city + international. Ad spend on top of retainer; the good news is local + WhatsApp is the cheapest CPL band in the logistics vertical."}}]}</script>
