    <section class="section">
        <div class="container">
            <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
            <p class="sec-sub">The real questions operators ask us before signing.</p>
            <div style="max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;">
            <div class="faq-item"><h3 class="faq-q">What is the single highest-ROI channel for a local courier company?</h3><div class="faq-a">Google Business Profile + local pack SEO. Zero marginal channel cost, high-intent buyers, and reviews compound trust. Most local courier operators under-invest in GBP optimisation and leave 30-50% of their local intent traffic on the table. We prioritise this in Phase 2 of every engagement.</div></div>
            <div class="faq-item"><h3 class="faq-q">How do local courier companies compete against Delhivery, Blue Dart and DTDC on Google?</h3><div class="faq-a">You do not compete for brand + national terms. You win on city + service + niche terms: "D2C courier Bhiwandi", "same-day delivery Whitefield", "documents courier Andheri". These win on local + long-tail SEO + Google Business Profile without needing D2C-scale ad budgets.</div></div>
            <div class="faq-item"><h3 class="faq-q">Should a courier company advertise on Meta (Facebook + Instagram)?</h3><div class="faq-a">Yes, if your customer includes D2C brand founders or small businesses. Meta targeting Shopify + WooCommerce merchants + Meta lookalikes on your best existing D2C clients is highly effective. Click-to-WhatsApp click-to-message ads reduce CPL by 30-40% vs form-fill for D2C 3PL and courier operators.</div></div>
            <div class="faq-item"><h3 class="faq-q">How does a courier company use WhatsApp for marketing?</h3><div class="faq-a">Three ways: (1) Click-to-message ads for lead capture from Meta + Google; (2) Booking + tracking + rate-broadcast + cross-sell flows via WhatsApp Cloud API + Interakt / AiSensy; (3) Automated review generation loop after every booking. This alone lifts NRR (net revenue retention) 20-40% on the existing customer book.</div></div>
            <div class="faq-item"><h3 class="faq-q">What is the CPL benchmark for courier leads on Google + Meta?</h3><div class="faq-a">Local courier enquiry Rs 60-200 per lead on Google Search Ads. D2C courier / 3PL enquiry Rs 350-800. Meta Ads for D2C-founder targeting Rs 400-1,200. Meta click-to-WhatsApp Rs 250-600. These are directional; SQL cost (qualified pipeline) is what matters for the P&amp;L.</div></div>
            <div class="faq-item"><h3 class="faq-q">How long does it take to see leads from courier company digital marketing?</h3><div class="faq-a">Google Business Profile + local pack: 30-45 days to visible movement. Paid channels: first leads in 5-10 days. SEO + content: month 3-4 for meaningful non-brand traffic. WhatsApp: immediate on launch of first broadcast. 60-80 leads / month is realistic for a well-executed 90-day launch on a mid-market local courier operator.</div></div>
            <div class="faq-item"><h3 class="faq-q">Do you help with franchise + partner marketing?</h3><div class="faq-a">Yes. For franchise networks, we build dedicated franchise-partner lead pages, multi-region SEO for hub coverage, partner-portal content, and franchise-onboarding funnels. Different funnel from customer acquisition; different KPIs; requires its own landing pages + creative + qualification form.</div></div>
            <div class="faq-item"><h3 class="faq-q">Can you handle international courier + cross-border marketing?</h3><div class="faq-a">Yes. India-to-GCC + India-to-USA + India-to-UK cross-border courier operators + document + parcel specialists. See our related freight-forwarding marketing page for the enterprise-B2B side; for D2C-facing international courier we mix Meta + WhatsApp with LinkedIn ABM.</div></div>
            <div class="faq-item"><h3 class="faq-q">What is the biggest mistake local courier companies make with marketing?</h3><div class="faq-a">Investing heavily in generic display + video ads before nailing Google Business Profile + local pack + review generation. Local courier is a discovery + trust business, not a brand-awareness business. Discovery + trust are cheaper + faster + more durable than paid awareness.</div></div>
            <div class="faq-item"><h3 class="faq-q">How much should a local courier company spend on digital marketing?</h3><div class="faq-a">Rs 1.5-3.5 lakh per month all-in for a founder-led local courier (Rs 3-20 Cr revenue). Rs 4-12 lakh for mid-market (Rs 20-150 Cr). Rs 12-40 lakh+ for enterprise + multi-city + international. Ad spend on top of retainer; the good news is local + WhatsApp is the cheapest CPL band in the logistics vertical.</div></div>
